post.description:
`RingCentral`'s sign-in page for the caller. `RingCentral` returns to
`/redirects/ringcentral/user-auth` with `code` and `state` (or `error`);
post them to `POST /v1/me/ringcentral` within 15 minutes.

delete.description:
Hides a stone of the caller's company from every list (soft delete;
nothing is erased). A stone that still has slabs in the yard needs
`include_slabs=true`, which hides those slabs too.

get.description:
Every company and its users with whether each may send documents for
signature (eSignatures are given per user, with no company switch);
`company_id` narrows the users to one company. Super admins only.

drive_note.description:
Why some drives are the job time rules' drive time rather than
Google's (no company address, no Google Maps, or too many stops);
null when every drive between addresses is Google's.

callKey.description:
The key that signs this browser's calls (`X-Granite-Call-Auth`, made
as the app makes it): base64url of 32 bytes. Keep it in memory only;
registering again gives it again.
